Jenkins install commands

if system already has ~.jenkins file, we wont get the admin password. 
If you see both Username and Password fields instead of a single "Administrator password" unlock box, Jenkins detected a pre-existing .jenkins folder in your home directory.


Option A: Start Completely Fresh (If you have no saved jobs)

1. Stop Jenkins in Terminal:bash
brew services stop jenkins-lts


Warning: Service `jenkins-lts` is not started.

That warning simply means Homebrew isn't currently running Jenkins, which makes it safe to delete the folder right away.

2.Delete the .jenkins folder:bash
rm -rf ~/.jenkins

3. Verify it is gone (this should return a "No such file or directory" message):bash
ls -la ~/.jenkins

3. Start Jenkins fresh (when you're ready to trigger the initial setup screen again):bash
brew services start jenkins-lts

